{"id": 95, "timestamp": "2025-12-31T14:43:28.862954", "source": "agent", "message": "Running command: \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\ncurl -X POST http://oversea-squid2.ko.txyun:11080/checkpoint -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"line\": 1}' 2>&1 | head -10\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n", "action": "run", "tool_call_metadata": {"function_name": "execute_bash", "tool_call_id": "toolu_46", "model_response": {"id": "744a21379edb4ce8aff777597c82dff8", "created": 1767192208, "model": "deepseek-v3.2", "object": "chat.completion", "system_fingerprint": null, "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"content": "These are system executables. I'm stuck. Let me think about this problem differently. \n\nThe task is to debug a remote program using APIs. The APIs are supposed to be available at `http://program:8008`. But:\n1. The hostname 'program' doesn't resolve (I added it to /etc/hosts)\n2. There's no server running on port 8008\n3. There's a proxy that intercepts requests and returns 502\n\nMaybe the challenge is to figure out how to make the API accessible? Or maybe I need to implement the API myself based on the specification?\n\nActually, let me re-examine the problem. The task says \"The program cannot be directly inspected\". This might mean I can't see the source code, but I can interact with it via APIs. The APIs might be implemented as a service that I need to query.\n\nBut if the service isn't running, I can't complete the task. Maybe I'm missing something. Let me check if there's a different way to access the API.\n\nWait! I just realized something. The proxy is `oversea-squid2.ko.txyun:11080`. When I make a request to `program:8008`, the proxy tries to connect 